{
  "id": "ss.relic.feed",
  "name": "Blood meal",
  "description": "A feeding head seen from the side — a dusky amber dome with two short antennae bent back and one dark palp — with its proboscis run out long and down to the right, and the tip sunk in a fat red drop that is the brightest thing on the plate. The pale tube carries a thread of red up its middle from the drop for half its length: blood on the way in, which is the whole relic — a kill feeds you. It is a bug mouth and not a straw in a glass because the tube grows out of a head, and the head is a plain dome with no eye and no dots on it, so it does not become a face. The drop is a solid bead with a coral crown rather than a hollow ring, which would have read as a bubble and put it next to ss.relic.venom.",
